message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EGFR Resistance Topology: Structural Footprints of Targeted-Therapy Resistance Mutations in the EGFR Kinase Pocket"
abstract: >-
  A topology-aware preliminary study quantifying how EGFR targeted-therapy
  (osimertinib) resistance mutations mark the drug-binding pocket. Per-residue
  structural deformation grades resistance mutations (L858R > T790M > C797S);
  C797S is structurally near-silent because its resistance is chemical (loss of
  the covalent anchor) rather than conformational.
type: software
authors:
